detail.longDescription:
Just realized: If you deploy Mastodon via Docker and proxy everything to `127.0.0.1:3000`, Rails is forced to read and stream all images & attachments from disk using `RAILS_SERVE_STATIC_FILES=true`. This has a massive performance impact. 

However, the host Nginx can serve all media directly with zero CPU/RAM overhead using kernel `sendfile`:

```nginx
location ^~ /system/ {
    root /srv/mastodon/data/public;
    add_header Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable";
    add_header X-Content-Type-Options nosniff;
    try_files $uri @mastodon_proxy;
}

location @mastodon_proxy {
    proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3000;
    proxy_set_header Host $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    # Security fix (GHSA-qp4r-p842-mw5c):
    proxy_set_header Forwarded "";
    proxy_set_header Proxy "";
}
```

